WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.379
- [Man] This program is about the only way

00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:06.626
of collecting meteorites

00:00:06.626 --> 00:00:09.751
in a very scientific and methodical way.

00:00:09.751 --> 00:00:11.688
You spend so much time preparing,

00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:12.737
once you get down there,

00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:16.442
you don't know whether
you can do this or not.

00:00:16.442 --> 00:00:18.163
And then the first time
you find a meteorite,

00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:20.663
you say, "Yes, I can do this."

00:00:26.565 --> 00:00:28.160
My name is Constantine Tsang.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.878
I'm at Southwest Research
Institute in Boulder, Colorado.

00:00:30.878 --> 00:00:34.642
I'm a planetary scientist
studying planetary atmospheres.

00:00:34.642 --> 00:00:36.998
We spent a total of two months on the ice.

00:00:36.998 --> 00:00:40.532
And we collected
approximately 569 meteorites.

00:00:40.532 --> 00:00:42.630
The scientific expedition's called ANSMET,

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.312
short for Antarctic Search for Meteorites.

00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:46.604
It's NASA-funded.

00:00:46.604 --> 00:00:47.568
And what we're trying to understand

00:00:47.568 --> 00:00:50.148
is how the formation of
the solar system began

00:00:50.148 --> 00:00:54.315
and how the planets evolved
to the way they look today.

00:00:56.493 --> 00:00:59.968
Tranquility, the beauty, the awesomeness,

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:04.051
there's no hyperbole that's
too great for Antarctica.

00:01:04.051 --> 00:01:06.563
The ice is crystal blue.

00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:08.063
The snow is thick.

00:01:08.906 --> 00:01:10.989
And the sun is brilliant.

00:01:12.032 --> 00:01:14.953
When we're on the ice
field, we live very basic.

00:01:14.953 --> 00:01:18.402
We live in tents with power
supplied by solar panels

00:01:18.402 --> 00:01:21.290
and chipping ice for water.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.834
The reason why we go to Antarctica

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:25.373
is because these are black
rocks on the white surface,

00:01:25.373 --> 00:01:27.378
so they're much easier to find.

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:29.964
As they go through the
atmosphere, they start to burn up,

00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:32.248
and they create this black fusion crust.

00:01:32.248 --> 00:01:35.757
And that's very distinct
from any terrestrial rock.

00:01:35.757 --> 00:01:37.386
By studying meteorites,
we're actually looking

00:01:37.386 --> 00:01:40.080
at the primordial history
of the solar system.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.830
This is a direct piece of evidence

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.113
how planets evolved and formed

00:01:44.113 --> 00:01:47.147
and how did life evolve on the Earth.

00:01:47.147 --> 00:01:48.697
No one gets to go out there

00:01:48.697 --> 00:01:51.454
except for scientists and very rich folk,

00:01:51.454 --> 00:01:53.822
so it was a huge privilege to go out

00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:57.739
and experience something
that is life-changing.

